{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyOV","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyOV","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalBaseExists"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.centralC2_acts_by_contentSqSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.centralC2_acts_by_contentSqSum","kind":"theorem","line":908,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L908-L948","doc":"**Punchline — `C₂` acts by `Σ_{c∈λ} c(c)²` on `S^λ`.** The Jucys–Murphy central element\n`C₂ = ∑_k X_k²` acts on the Specht module `S^λ ≤ M^λ` (via `Specht.Mtab.rep` extended to the group\nalgebra) as the **scalar** `contentSqSum μ`.  That is, for every `x ∈ S^λ`,\n`ρ(C₂) · x = (contentSqSum μ) • x`.\n\nThis is the central element acting by a single eigenvalue on the irreducible `S^λ` (Schur's lemma\nmade explicit): since each `X_k` acts on the seminormal vector for `T` by `c(cell of k)`, the\ncentral `∑_k X_k²` acts by `∑_k c(cell of k)² = ∑_{c∈λ} c(c)²` — independent of `T`, hence a\nscalar on all of `S^λ`.  **This integer scalar `contentSqSum μ` is exactly the `ω = Σc²` field of\nthe keystone's `SnWedderburnSpectralData`** (`QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace`); discharging\nthis theorem discharges that field's content for the Specht-module block.\n\n**Sorry-free modulo the two cited OV cores.** The proof is a `Submodule.span_induction`:\nthe seminormal vectors span `S^λ` (`seminormalVectors_span`), `C₂` acts on each by `contentSqSum μ`\n(the sorry-free `centralC2_smul_seminormal`), and the scalar action extends through `+`, `0`, and\n`k`-scaling because both `ρ(C₂)` and `(contentSqSum μ) • ·` are `k`-linear.  No `sorry`, no `ℝ`,\nno `native_decide`.\n\n**Base ring `[Field k] [CharZero k]`** — inherited from `seminormalVectors_span` (the completeness it\nconsumes is false over `ℤ`; see that lemma).  The capstone uses this at `k := R` with\n`[Field R] [CharZero R]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.seminormalVectors_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.seminormalVectors_span","kind":"theorem","line":879,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L879-L906","doc":"**Seminormal vectors span the Specht module (Okounkov–Vershik) — sorry-free modulo the single\nindependence core `exists_indep_seminormal_family`.** The Specht submodule `S^λ ≤ M^λ` is contained in\nthe span of the seminormal (Gelfand–Zetlin) vectors; with the automatic reverse inclusion\n`seminormalSpan_le`, the GZ vectors span `S^λ`.  This is the OV completeness consumed by the punchline\n`centralC2_acts_by_contentSqSum` (the scalar action propagates from the spanning vectors by\n`Submodule.span_induction`).\n\n**De-abstraction.** `span ≤ S^λ` (`seminormalSpan_le`) plus `dim S^λ = #SYT(μ) ≤ dim(span)` (the\ncounting plumbing over the independence core) force `span = S^λ` on the finite-dimensional `M^λ`\n(`Submodule.eq_of_le_of_finrank_le`); take `.ge`.  So the cited debt is now *independence of the\nseminormal family* only — strictly more atomic than the old whole-inclusion `sorry`.\n\n**Base ring — `[Field k] [CharZero k]` (§7c over-generality fix).** Completeness is false over `ℤ`\n(seminormal vectors carry denominators ⇒ the integral vectors span only a proper finite-index\nsublattice) and the independence is false in positive characteristic (contents collide mod `p`), so\nthe char-0 field is the honest generality.  The `[CommRing k]` form would be an over-general cited\nclaim — the same anti-pattern as `DominanceData.dom_colStab`; the capstone consumes the punchline at a\nchar-0 field `R`, so the restriction costs nothing downstream. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.numSYT_le_finrank_seminormalSpan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.numSYT_le_finrank_seminormalSpan","kind":"theorem","line":861,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L861-L877","doc":"**Plumbing (sorry-free): `#SYT(μ) ≤ dim_k(span)`.** The span of the independent `#SYT(μ)`-family\nalready has dimension `#SYT(μ)` (`finrank_span_eq_card`), and it is contained in `seminormalSpan`\n(`Submodule.finrank_mono`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.exists_indep_seminormal_family","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.exists_indep_seminormal_family","kind":"theorem","line":813,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L813-L859","doc":"**The atomic OV completeness core (Young's seminormal form, independence half) — now assembled,\nnot cited.** The seminormal (Gelfand–Zetlin) vectors form a **linearly independent** family indexed\nby **all** standard Young tableaux of shape `μ` — i.e. `#SYT(μ) = dim S^λ`-many independent\nsimultaneous JM-eigenvectors.\n\n**De-abstraction (this proof is sorry-free; its only cited input is the existence core).** The\nfamily is built by choice from `seminormalVector_data_exists` (the eigenvector existence core);\nindependence is the generic joint-eigenvalue argument `linearIndependent_of_joint_eigenvectors`\n(L1, proved) applied to the operators `ρ(X_s)` with eigenvalue tuples the cast content vectors\n`s ↦ ((cellContent (cell of s in T) : ℤ) : k)`, whose injectivity is `Int.cast_injective`\n(`CharZero`) + the combinatorial simple-spectrum fact `syt_content_tuple_injective` (L2 —\n**proved**, via the diagonal row-count formula).  So the entire cited debt of this statement is\n`seminormalVector_data_exists` — both the linear algebra and the spectrum combinatorics are\nmachine-checked.\n\nThis is strictly more atomic than the old `seminormalVectors_span` cited `sorry`: that cited the\nwhole inclusion `S^λ ⊆ span`; the *spanning* is a sorry-free dimension corollary\n(`seminormalVectors_span` below), and the independence is now itself assembled from more atomic\nparts.\n\n**Base ring `[Field k] [CharZero k]`** (not over-general): in positive characteristic the cell\ncontents collide mod `p`, merging eigenspaces and breaking distinctness, so the `[CommRing k]` form\nwould be false at its generality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.syt_content_tuple_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.syt_content_tuple_injective","kind":"theorem","line":755,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L755-L811","doc":"**(L2) The seminormal simple-spectrum core (combinatorial): the content tuple determines the\nstandard tableau — PROVED.** If two standard Young tableaux of shape `μ` assign the same\ncell-content to every label, they are equal.\n\nProof (no diagram-removal): entries strictly increase along each diagonal\n(`entry_lt_of_diag_row_lt`), so the **row** of the cell holding label `s` is\n`(−content s)⁺ + #{s' < s with the same content}` (`row_eq_offset_add_count`) — a function of the\ncontent tuple alone, hence shared by `T` and `T'`.  The **column** then follows from\nrow + content, so the label→cell maps coincide; inverting, the cell→label maps (`cellLabel`)\ncoincide, i.e. all entries agree on `μ` (and off `μ` both are pinned to `0`), so `T = T'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.linearIndependent_of_joint_eigenvectors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.linearIndependent_of_joint_eigenvectors","kind":"theorem","line":507,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L507-L585","doc":"**(L1) Joint eigenvectors with pairwise-distinct eigenvalue tuples are linearly independent.**\nGeneric linear algebra (no tableau/Specht content, sorry-free): a family `v : ι → V` of nonzero\nvectors, each a simultaneous eigenvector of every operator `A s` with eigenvalue tuple\n`c i : S → k`; if the tuple map `c` is injective, the family is independent.\n\nProof: `linearIndependent_iff'` + strong induction on the support `t` of a finite dependency.  For\n`j ∈ t`: if `t = {j}`, then `g j • v j = 0` forces `g j = 0` (`v j ≠ 0`); otherwise pick `i₀ ∈ t`\nwith `i₀ ≠ j` and a separator `s₀` with `c i₀ s₀ ≠ c j s₀` (tuple injectivity), apply `A s₀` and\nsubtract `c i₀ s₀ ·` the original relation — the `i₀` term dies, and the inductive hypothesis on\n`t.erase i₀` gives `g j · (c j s₀ − c i₀ s₀) = 0`, whence `g j = 0`.\n\nNote the operators need **not** commute and no diagonalisability is assumed — only the given\nfamily's eigen-structure is used.  This is the entire linear-algebra content of the OV\n\"distinct content-tuples ⇒ independent\" step, factored out of the citation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.seminormalSpan_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.seminormalSpan_le","kind":"theorem","line":499,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L499-L505","doc":"**Easy direction (sorry-free).** The seminormal span sits inside `S^λ` — every seminormal vector\nlies in `S^λ` (the `mem` field of `SeminormalVector`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.seminormalSpan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.seminormalSpan","kind":"def","line":493,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L493-L497","doc":"The span of the seminormal vectors, as a submodule of `M^λ` (local abbreviation; the public\n`seminormalVectors_span` below uses the inline `Submodule.span …` form for splice-compatibility). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.jucysMurphy_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.jucysMurphy_eigenvalue","kind":"theorem","line":462,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L462-L491","doc":"**Jucys–Murphy eigenvalue theorem (Okounkov–Vershik).** The Specht module `S^λ` admits a\nGelfand–Zetlin / seminormal basis indexed by the standard Young tableaux of shape `μ`, on which\nevery JM element `X_k` acts **diagonally** with eigenvalue `cellContent (cell of k in T)`.\n\nWe state this as: for every standard tableau `T` of shape `μ`, there is a seminormal eigenvector\n`sv` whose indexing tableau is `T`.  The eigenproperty itself is recorded as the `isEig` field of\n`SeminormalVector` (each `X_k` acts by the content of `k`'s cell); the *content* of the theorem is\nthe **existence** of such vectors for every `T`, i.e. that the GZ basis exists and diagonalises the\nJM elements.  Together with `jucysMurphy_commute`, this is the heart of the OV approach.\n\n**Reduction (sorry-free here, modulo the named eigenvector core).** This theorem no longer carries\nthe `sorry` directly.  Its `cellOf` field is *constructed* from `T` by the sorry-free brick-4\nbijection `tableauCellEquiv μ T` (= `sytToTableau T`), and the eigenvector data `(v, mem, nz, isEig)`\nis supplied by `seminormalVector_data_exists` — the single cited core that isolates exactly Young's\nseminormal-vector existence.  `sv.T = T` then holds by `rfl`.  So the genuine OV debt is now named\nprecisely (`seminormalVector_data_exists`) and the *bijection* part — historically bundled into the\nsame `sorry` — is genuinely closed.\n\n**Base ring `[Field k] [CharZero k]`** — inherited from `seminormalVector_data_exists` (the\nseminormal eigenvector is a char-0 fact; the `[CommRing k]` form is over-general, false at `ℤ/pℤ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.seminormalVector_data_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.seminormalVector_data_exists","kind":"theorem","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L427-L460","doc":"**The Okounkov–Vershik existence theorem (Young's seminormal vector), de-abstracted.** For\nevery standard Young tableau `T` of shape `μ`, there exists a nonzero vector `v` in the Specht\nsubmodule `S^λ` on which **each** Jucys–Murphy element `X_s` acts diagonally with eigenvalue\n`cellContent (c)`, where `c = tableauCellEquiv μ T s` is the cell of `μ` holding label `s` in `T`.\n\n**De-abstraction (this proof is sorry-free; its inputs are the two named cores).** Take the base\nseminormal vector (`seminormalVector_base_exists`, core 1), walk the admissible-adjacent-swap\nchain from its tableau to `T` (`syt_adjacentSwap_connected`, core 2), transporting the\neigenvector along each step by the machine-checked classical 2×2 seminormal block\n(`seminormalVector_data_step`: the JM recursion `s·X_a·s = X_b − s` + the eigenvalue-swap /\nfixed-operator / non-vanishing linear algebra + `S^λ`-invariance — all sorry-free).  The cited\ndebt is thus reduced from \"all-`T` eigenvector existence\" to {base-tableau existence,\nadjacent-swap connectivity} — each strictly more atomic.\n\n**Base ring `[Field k] [CharZero k]` (§7c over-generality fix).** Stated over a char-0 field, NOT\nthe file-wide `[CommRing k]`: over a general commutative ring the integer cell-contents can collide\nmodulo the characteristic (e.g. `ℤ/pℤ` with `c_i ≡ c_j` but `c_i ≠ c_j`), so the cast JM eigenvalues\n`↑c_s` stop being distinct, the eigenspaces merge, and a simultaneous eigenvector with the\n*prescribed* content tuple need not exist in `S^λ` — the `[CommRing k]` form is over-general (false at\n`ℤ/pℤ`).  Young's seminormal form is genuinely a char-0 fact (it inverts the content differences\n`c_i − c_j`, exactly as the transport step does). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.syt_adjacentSwap_connected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.syt_adjacentSwap_connected","kind":"theorem","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L413-L425","doc":"**OV existence core 2 (adjacent-swap connectivity of standard tableaux — combinatorial).**\nAny two standard Young tableaux of the same shape are connected by a chain of admissible\nadjacent swaps (`AdjacentSwapStep`).\n\n**De-abstraction (this proof is sorry-free).** Both `T` and `T'` connect to the common base `T₀`\n(`syt_all_connect_to_some`, core 2); reverse the second leg by symmetry\n(`reflTransGen_adjacentSwap_symm`) and compose (`T ⤳* T₀ ⤳* T'`). The residual cited debt is thus\nthe strictly smaller one-directional base walk, with the two-directional plumbing proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.syt_all_connect_to_some","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.syt_all_connect_to_some","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L360-L411","doc":"**OV existence core 2 — every standard tableau walks to the row-superstandard base\n(sorry-free).** Well-founded induction on the inversion count of `π_T`: at `0` inversions `π_T = 1`\nso `T = T₀`; otherwise an adjacent descent of `π_T` yields (`descent_ne_row`/`descent_ne_col`) an\nadmissible swap (`adjacentSwapStep_swapCells`) whose result has strictly smaller inversion count\n(`permOf_swapCells` + `invCount_mul_swap_lt`), so the induction closes the walk. Every descent is\nadmissible because same-row / same-column consecutive labels map to *ascents* under\n`cellLabel_{T₀}`, and consecutive labels never share a diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.permOf_swapCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.permOf_swapCells","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L309-L358","doc":"The swap of two adjacent-label cells right-multiplies `π_T` by `swap a b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.descent_ne_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.descent_ne_col","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L275-L307","doc":"A descent of `π_T` at adjacent labels forces the two cells into different columns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.descent_ne_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.descent_ne_row","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L241-L273","doc":"A descent of `π_T` at adjacent labels forces the two cells into different rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.eq_of_tableauCellEquiv_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.eq_of_tableauCellEquiv_eq","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L224-L239","doc":"A standard tableau is determined by its label→cell bijection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.permOf_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.permOf_base","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L219-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.permOf_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.permOf_val","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L212-L217","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.permOf_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.permOf_apply","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L206-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.permOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.permOf","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L199-L204","doc":"The permutation `π_T = cellLabel_{T₀} ∘ tableauCellEquiv_T` of `Fin (nOf μ)`; `= 1` at `T₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.baseTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.baseTableau","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L195-L197","doc":"The base tableau for the exchange walk: the row-superstandard tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.adjacentSwapStep_swapCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.adjacentSwapStep_swapCells","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L137-L191","doc":"**Realization of an admissible adjacent swap (sorry-free).** For adjacent labels `a, a+1`\nwhose cells in `T` lie in different rows and columns, the consecutive-label cell-swap tableau\n`swapCellsSYT` realizes an `AdjacentSwapStep μ T ·`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.tableauCellEquiv_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.tableauCellEquiv_mem","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L131-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.entry_tableauCellEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.entry_tableauCellEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L123-L129","doc":"The entry at the cell of label `s` is `s` itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.tableauCellEquiv_cellLabel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.tableauCellEquiv_cellLabel","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L117-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.cellLabel_tableauCellEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.cellLabel_tableauCellEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L111-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.reflTransGen_adjacentSwap_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.reflTransGen_adjacentSwap_symm","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L100-L109","doc":"**The admissible-adjacent-swap chain relation is symmetric (sorry-free).** Immediate from\n`adjacentSwapStep_symm` by induction on the chain (reverse each step). Hence\n`Relation.ReflTransGen (AdjacentSwapStep μ)` is an equivalence relation on `SYT(μ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.adjacentSwapStep_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.adjacentSwapStep_symm","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L82-L98","doc":"**`AdjacentSwapStep` is symmetric (sorry-free).** Swapping `a, a+1` back in `T'` returns `T`:\nthe content-swap conditions are visibly symmetric in `T ↔ T'`, and the content gap only changes\n*sign* under the swap (`c'_b − c'_a = c_a − c_b = −(c_b − c_a)`), so the admissibility conditions\n`d ≠ 0` and `d² ≠ 1` survive (`omega` / `(a−b)² = (b−a)²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.seminormalVector_base_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy.seminormalVector_base_exists","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyOV.lean#L31-L80","doc":"**OV existence core 1 (base seminormal vector — the residual cited debt).** For *some*\nstandard tableau `T₀` of shape `μ` there is a nonzero simultaneous JM eigenvector in `S^λ`\nwith the content tuple of `T₀`.  Classically this is the explicit seminormal vector of the\ncolumn-superstandard tableau (or, in Okounkov–Vershik, the highest weight of the GZ chain).\n\n**Status note (corrected).** An earlier version of this docstring said the construction \"needs\nthe polytabloid straightening machinery not yet built here\". That is **stale**: this file\nimports `QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis`, and the straightening machinery\n(`standardPolytabloid_straightening`, `standardPolytabloid_span`, and the Garnir core\n`straightening_step_colMax`) is now **proved sorry-free** there — `#print axioms` on each gives\nexactly `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`. So the cited blocker no longer applies; what\nremains is the eigen-computation itself, not missing infrastructure.\n\nThe reduction is set up in `QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector` (sorry-free, imports this\nfile — hence the residual must be discharged there or in a leaf, not in place). Its\n`jm_polytabloid_split` gives, for any tableau `t`,\n\n  `X_s · e_t = #{j < s : (j s) ∈ colStab t} · (−e_t) + Σ_{j < s, (j s) ∉ colStab t} e_{(j s)·t}`.\n\nFor the column-superstandard `T₀` with `s` at cell `(i, j)` the same-column count is `i`, so the\nfirst term is `−i · e_{T₀}`; since `content(i,j) = j − i`, the **sole remaining obligation** is\nthe off-column (Garnir) collapse\n\n  `Σ_{j' < s, (j' s) ∉ colStab T₀} e_{(j' s)·T₀} = j · e_{T₀}`,\n\ni.e. the off-column sum contributes exactly the number of cells strictly left of `s` in its row.\nNumerically confirmed in\n`docs/audits/2026-07-19-ov-base-vector-column-superstandard-verification.md`.\n\nStrictly\nsmaller than the previous all-`T` existence core: existence for a *single* tableau, with the\npropagation to every `T` now machine-checked (`seminormalVector_data_step` +\n`syt_adjacentSwap_connected`).\n\n**Base ring `[Field k] [CharZero k]`** — see `seminormalVector_data_exists`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}